A||||2||ponya||Lower quarter panel repair||||5||
Z||000000||ponya||07-23-2000||10:29 PM||||I have a bodywork question. I have a lower rear quarter panel that has a gash in it. There is no hole, just a gash approx. 3" long. Can you use regular Bondo to repair it or do you have to use fiber glass repair. I have a lot of experience with the regular bondo and none using fiberglass. Will the regular stick etc? Any information appreciated. Thanks,  Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||07-24-2000||06:04 AM||||Use flexable body filler available at most automotive paint supply places. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||07-24-2000||10:24 PM||||The stuff I have had the best results with is called Flexible Sem Weld.  It is made by Sem Products, Inc. 651 Michael Wylie Drive, Charlotte, NC  28217. Ph.#704-522-1006; order desk: 800-831-1122;fax# 704-522-7008.  You should be able to get it at any auto paint supply house, like Phil said.<P>Have a good one! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
